1
00:00:00,568 --> 00:00:02,656
This is Souta Kobayakawa. My boyfriend.

2
00:00:02,656 --> 00:00:03,680
Tutor?

3
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:05,906
Go, Rock!

4
00:00:05,906 --> 00:00:07,074
How about calling him
'Nat' as a middle ground?

5
00:00:07,074 --> 00:00:08,242
Nat...

6
00:00:08,242 --> 00:00:09,810
It's fine, you can call me whatever.

7
00:00:09,810 --> 00:00:11,679
You like clouds, don't you?

8
00:00:11,679 --> 00:00:14,448
<i>I'm not feeling nervous or anything.</i>

9
00:00:14,448 --> 00:00:17,250
<i>Definitely not.</i>

10
00:00:24,544 --> 00:00:27,208
[Episode 3]

11
00:00:36,270 --> 00:00:37,850
<i>Ever since I was little,</i>

12
00:00:37,850 --> 00:00:41,374
<i>I've tended to like
the same things my sister likes.</i>

13
00:00:46,368 --> 00:00:50,718
<i>When she started dancing,
I wanted to start dancing too.</i>

14
00:00:50,718 --> 00:00:52,128
- You too, Natsuki?
- <i>I also liked her favorite manga,</i>

15
00:00:52,128 --> 00:00:53,900
- Yeah, cool.
- <i>and even the same anime characters too.</i>

16
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:55,540
- Stop copying me.
- I'm not.

17
00:00:55,540 --> 00:00:57,360
I just happen to like the same ones you do.

18
00:00:58,259 --> 00:01:02,696
<i>But when it comes to the guys she dates,
I've never been impressed.</i>

19
00:01:02,696 --> 00:01:06,300
<i>A shady-looking guy who looks like
he's about to punch someone.</i>

20
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:09,248
<i>A foreigner with zero
Japanese communication skills.</i>

21
00:01:09,248 --> 00:01:12,373
<i>An unsociable senior
who never cracks a smile.</i>

22
00:01:12,373 --> 00:01:13,720
<i>So this time too,</i>

23
00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:15,136
- Riyo, over here!
- <i>at first, I thought he was</i>

24
00:01:15,136 --> 00:01:17,352
<i>a smug, insufferable jerk.</i>

25
00:01:18,045 --> 00:01:19,679
<i>But...</i>

26
00:01:20,547 --> 00:01:22,940
If you do this here...

27
00:01:22,940 --> 00:01:26,153
<i>Little by little, I started to think
he might be a good guy.</i>

28
00:01:26,153 --> 00:01:29,023
- Are you listening?
- <i>We got a little closer, bit by bit.</i>

29
00:01:29,023 --> 00:01:31,040
Is it okay if I talk about myself?

30
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:32,293
<i>Little by little...</i>

31
00:01:32,293 --> 00:01:35,200
Nat!

32
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:37,564
<i>Little by little...</i>

33
00:01:37,564 --> 00:01:39,366
<i>Hmm?</i>

34
00:01:39,366 --> 00:01:42,469
<i>Little by little... what?</i>

35
00:01:42,469 --> 00:01:45,105
Natsuki, want more watermelon?

36
00:01:45,105 --> 00:01:49,340
<i>What's this feeling?</i>

37
00:01:49,340 --> 00:01:51,241
Natsuki?

38
00:01:59,787 --> 00:02:01,888
[Someone looks like he's sparkling]

39
00:02:01,888 --> 00:02:03,424
[A sign of a migraine or an eye problem?]

40
00:02:03,424 --> 00:02:05,000
What?

41
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:09,203
<i>A sign of a migraine or an eye problem?</i>

42
00:02:10,680 --> 00:02:12,982
Hey!

43
00:02:17,504 --> 00:02:20,540
[Love]

44
00:02:20,540 --> 00:02:22,808
- Lo...
- Lo?

45
00:02:25,346 --> 00:02:28,360
<i>No, no, no, no, no, no!</i>

46
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:30,080
<i>He's my sister's boyfriend!</i>

47
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:32,600
Hello?

48
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:35,680
- You scared me!
- No, that's my line.

49
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:38,425
What's wrong? Are you feeling sick?

50
00:02:38,425 --> 00:02:40,440
No, I'm fine.

51
00:02:40,440 --> 00:02:43,260
But you've been acting strange.

52
00:02:43,260 --> 00:02:44,498
Really?

53
00:02:44,498 --> 00:02:46,308
You were muttering to yourself,

54
00:02:46,308 --> 00:02:49,360
and almost picked up the watermelon,
but then stopped.

55
00:02:49,360 --> 00:02:51,552
And you were also making
all sorts of weird faces.

56
00:02:51,552 --> 00:02:55,642
- Was I doing that?
- Do you have a fever from studying too much?

57
00:02:55,642 --> 00:02:57,952
- Huh?
- You suddenly started studying so hard,

58
00:02:57,952 --> 00:02:59,213
your body's in shock.

59
00:02:59,213 --> 00:03:01,240
Maybe you have a fever?

60
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:03,684
- I'm not a kid.
- Oh, watermelon!

61
00:03:03,684 --> 00:03:06,184
- I'll take it!
- Hey, wait!

62
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:12,092
- So good!
- I was about to eat that.

63
00:03:12,092 --> 00:03:14,161
There's more.

64
00:03:14,161 --> 00:03:15,863
Riyo, are you going out?

65
00:03:15,863 --> 00:03:17,200
Yeah, on a date.

66
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:20,067
- With Souta?
- Yes.

67
00:03:20,067 --> 00:03:23,470
I heard that you still can't
call him 'Sou', right, Natsuki?

68
00:03:23,470 --> 00:03:26,907
Souta said that he started
calling you 'Nat', though.

69
00:03:26,907 --> 00:03:30,176
Nat!

70
00:03:30,778 --> 00:03:34,144
It's just first names,
so you don't have to be so shy about it.

71
00:03:34,144 --> 00:03:36,600
I'm not shy.

72
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:37,992
Okay, okay, here you go.

73
00:03:38,652 --> 00:03:40,320
Thanks.

74
00:03:41,422 --> 00:03:43,056
Coming.

75
00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:55,169
Souta and I are going to
the National Museum of Western Art today.

76
00:03:55,169 --> 00:03:57,120
Cool.

77
00:03:57,120 --> 00:04:02,175
Souta didn't even know that
it's a World Heritage Site.

78
00:04:02,843 --> 00:04:05,056
I mean, he seems to know everything,

79
00:04:05,056 --> 00:04:07,592
but he's surprisingly clueless
about some things.

80
00:04:09,683 --> 00:04:11,919
I bet he knows a lot
about the things he likes, right?

81
00:04:11,919 --> 00:04:13,184
Oh, yeah, yeah!

82
00:04:13,184 --> 00:04:18,258
When it comes to his beloved bridges,
he's like a walking encyclopedia.

83
00:04:18,258 --> 00:04:20,661
He starts talking a mile a minute.

84
00:04:20,661 --> 00:04:23,864
Bridges span rivers, seas, valleys, roads,

85
00:04:23,864 --> 00:04:26,664
connecting places that are otherwise divided.

86
00:04:28,001 --> 00:04:30,216
Well, that's what makes him cute.

87
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:33,760
Cute, huh?

88
00:04:33,760 --> 00:04:35,928
Souta's cute, right?

89
00:04:38,100 --> 00:04:41,648
Kaoru brought some bread from the shop.

90
00:04:41,648 --> 00:04:43,584
Want to take some on your date, Riyo?

91
00:04:43,584 --> 00:04:44,768
Oh, maybe I should.

92
00:04:44,768 --> 00:04:47,488
- You can pick your favorite.
- Yay!

93
00:04:47,488 --> 00:04:49,480
Oh, look.

94
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:51,983
- Oh, melon!
- Wow, there's so much!

95
00:04:51,983 --> 00:04:55,232
- Looks delicious.
- Where should we eat it?

96
00:04:55,232 --> 00:04:58,232
We're going to see a bridge
after we visit the museum.

97
00:04:58,232 --> 00:04:59,566
- A bridge?
- Yeah.

98
00:04:59,566 --> 00:05:02,035
I was just telling Natsuki about it.

99
00:05:02,035 --> 00:05:05,038
Souta loves bridges
and knows a ton about them.

100
00:05:05,038 --> 00:05:06,912
- That's unusual.
- It is, isn't it?

101
00:05:06,912 --> 00:05:11,345
I feel like there's a history and romance
connected to World Heritage Sites.

102
00:05:11,345 --> 00:05:13,160
I see.

103
00:05:13,160 --> 00:05:17,718
Oh, and also, Souta says he wants to
build bridges in the future.

104
00:05:17,718 --> 00:05:20,320
Oh, that's so cool!

105
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:22,389
He even chose our university,

106
00:05:22,389 --> 00:05:25,359
apparently because there's
a famous architecture professor.

107
00:05:25,359 --> 00:05:28,996
I see. Even cooler.

108
00:05:28,996 --> 00:05:30,440
Oh! The pot, the pot!

109
00:05:34,868 --> 00:05:36,296
Hey.

110
00:05:38,580 --> 00:05:41,120
Stuff about his dreams
and other personal stuff.

111
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:43,820
Shouldn't you not talk about that
when he's not around?

112
00:05:43,820 --> 00:05:45,820
What? Really?

113
00:05:45,820 --> 00:05:50,390
He might have only told you that
because you're his girlfriend.

114
00:05:53,086 --> 00:05:54,654
I see.

115
00:05:56,768 --> 00:05:59,688
I suppose I do tend to blab about everything,

116
00:05:59,688 --> 00:06:02,280
so I don't always notice that stuff.

117
00:06:03,630 --> 00:06:05,160
Thanks for telling me.

118
00:06:08,769 --> 00:06:10,792
- Thanks!
- Hey, cut it out!

119
00:06:11,648 --> 00:06:15,200
- Don't be shy, don't be shy!
- Get off!

120
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:17,000
Hey, that's my T-shirt!

121
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:18,880
- It suits me, right?
- Don't just wear it without asking.

122
00:06:18,880 --> 00:06:20,347
But I like it.

123
00:06:20,347 --> 00:06:21,504
It's mine.

124
00:06:21,504 --> 00:06:22,820
[Open]

125
00:06:22,820 --> 00:06:24,820
[Closed]

126
00:06:24,820 --> 00:06:26,000
- Go, go, go!
- Whoa, whoa!

127
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:28,855
- Yeah!
- What the heck?

128
00:06:28,855 --> 00:06:30,656
- Darn it!
- Look, see this?

129
00:06:30,656 --> 00:06:32,620
Natsuki, shouldn't you be studying?

130
00:06:32,620 --> 00:06:34,995
Don't you start. Come on, help me out!

131
00:06:34,995 --> 00:06:36,530
I need a break sometimes.

132
00:06:36,530 --> 00:06:37,965
My tutor comes at night anyway.

133
00:06:37,965 --> 00:06:40,968
Speaking of which, your tutor
doesn't seem like such a bad guy.

134
00:06:40,968 --> 00:06:43,103
What? You met him?

135
00:06:43,103 --> 00:06:45,352
We saw you guys the other day.

136
00:06:46,006 --> 00:06:47,975
We saw you two together.

137
00:06:47,975 --> 00:06:49,609
What?

138
00:06:50,477 --> 00:06:52,546
<i>You seemed to be having fun, Natsuki.</i>

139
00:06:52,546 --> 00:06:55,849
Yeah, yeah. Like good buddies!

140
00:06:55,849 --> 00:06:59,688
What? No way. That's not true at all.

141
00:07:02,990 --> 00:07:04,820
Sorry for the wait!

142
00:07:04,820 --> 00:07:06,927
Not at all.

143
00:07:06,927 --> 00:07:08,168
Let's go.

144
00:07:09,496 --> 00:07:12,192
- I'm so excited.
- Yeah, it'll be fun.

145
00:07:12,192 --> 00:07:14,088
Okay.

146
00:07:15,702 --> 00:07:17,480
Souta.

147
00:07:18,305 --> 00:07:19,972
This way, this way.

148
00:07:21,856 --> 00:07:25,096
Oh right, the other way.

149
00:07:27,681 --> 00:07:29,920
You can't read a map, can you?

150
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:32,820
That's not true. It was just a coincidence.

151
00:07:32,820 --> 00:07:35,722
- You really are clueless.
- I am not.

152
00:07:35,722 --> 00:07:37,256
I meant, you're cute.

153
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:40,552
Cu... Cute?

154
00:07:44,564 --> 00:07:48,064
- What do you mean, "cute"?
- Just what I said.

155
00:07:48,064 --> 00:07:51,232
- I'm home. Oh, Rock!
- Welcome back.

156
00:07:51,232 --> 00:07:53,320
How was the soba-making class?

157
00:07:54,207 --> 00:07:55,784
It was okay.

158
00:07:56,610 --> 00:07:59,520
Could it be a hobby for your retirement?

159
00:07:59,520 --> 00:08:01,048
I'm not sure yet.

160
00:08:01,048 --> 00:08:03,984
Huh? What about Fuku? Did he do okay?

161
00:08:03,984 --> 00:08:07,320
He had the teacher do
almost everything for him.

162
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:11,591
Oh, that guy. He's such a sly one.

163
00:08:12,559 --> 00:08:15,562
Are the kids out?

164
00:08:15,562 --> 00:08:18,080
- Yeah.
- Natsuki too?

165
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:20,600
Yes, he does need a break sometimes.

166
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:23,904
Can he really afford to be so laid-back?

167
00:08:23,904 --> 00:08:29,109
Well, Souta said that
Natsuki's been working really hard,

168
00:08:29,109 --> 00:08:32,192
and that he picks things up quickly.

169
00:08:32,192 --> 00:08:33,680
Really?

170
00:08:33,680 --> 00:08:37,984
I'm so glad Riyo introduced us
to such a good teacher.

171
00:08:37,984 --> 00:08:39,686
They're close in age too.

172
00:08:39,686 --> 00:08:42,560
And they're guys,
so they probably get along well.

173
00:08:42,560 --> 00:08:44,072
Yeah, probably.

174
00:08:48,595 --> 00:08:53,400
Your ramen and gyoza really
are the best in the world, sir.

175
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:55,035
No, the best in the world
is the fried chicken.

176
00:08:55,035 --> 00:08:57,771
You guys don't know enough about the world.

177
00:08:57,771 --> 00:09:01,074
- Natsuki and Ryo, you really get my cooking.
- Yeah, yeah.

178
00:09:01,074 --> 00:09:02,809
Unlike my idiot son.

179
00:09:02,809 --> 00:09:05,812
- What? Idiot son?
- Just be honest, man.

180
00:09:05,812 --> 00:09:07,380
- Yeah.
- Shut up.

181
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:09,282
It's so good that I could eat it every day.

182
00:09:09,282 --> 00:09:11,017
You're definitely siblings.

183
00:09:11,017 --> 00:09:13,253
Riyo said the same thing the other day.

184
00:09:13,253 --> 00:09:15,140
What?

185
00:09:15,140 --> 00:09:16,757
- Delicious.
- Delicious.

186
00:09:16,757 --> 00:09:19,059
I want to eat this every day, it's so good!

187
00:09:19,059 --> 00:09:21,056
And she actually came two days in a row.

188
00:09:21,056 --> 00:09:22,729
Apparently, she came
with a guy the second day.

189
00:09:22,729 --> 00:09:24,765
- Huh? Really?
- Oh, is that so?

190
00:09:24,765 --> 00:09:26,664
I wasn't there, but you said so.

191
00:09:27,968 --> 00:09:29,416
Did she come with her boyfriend?

192
00:09:30,900 --> 00:09:33,440
I can't disclose the personal
information of my customers.

193
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:36,128
It's part of the service industry code.

194
00:09:36,128 --> 00:09:38,945
- Cool.
- Come on. Just say you don't remember.

195
00:09:38,945 --> 00:09:42,048
Oh, was it Natsuki's tutor?

196
00:09:42,048 --> 00:09:46,052
The guy she came with,
was he like a smiling, refreshing ghost?

197
00:09:46,052 --> 00:09:47,788
Yes, something like that.

198
00:09:47,788 --> 00:09:49,088
You called him a refreshing ghost?

199
00:09:49,088 --> 00:09:52,180
- You're funny, Natsuki.
- No way he said that.

200
00:09:52,180 --> 00:09:53,760
- Well, sort of.
- Gyoza, the best in the world!

201
00:09:53,760 --> 00:09:54,828
They're just good.

202
00:09:54,828 --> 00:09:59,566
<i>So coming to realize
that they came here on a date,</i>

203
00:09:59,566 --> 00:10:02,034
<i>I felt disappointed?</i>

204
00:10:03,270 --> 00:10:05,071
<i>Why?</i>

205
00:10:14,014 --> 00:10:17,050
<i>You like clouds, don't you?</i>

206
00:10:17,050 --> 00:10:20,987
Argh, why is that popping up?

207
00:10:20,987 --> 00:10:23,857
Get out of my head.

208
00:10:23,857 --> 00:10:25,958
Nat!

209
00:10:26,693 --> 00:10:29,000
I said, shut up!

210
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,934
Nat!

211
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:35,569
What?

212
00:10:35,569 --> 00:10:37,203
Hang on a sec.

213
00:10:37,804 --> 00:10:39,805
It was real.

214
00:10:44,845 --> 00:10:46,579
Perfect timing.

215
00:10:47,781 --> 00:10:49,549
Huh? Where's my sister?

216
00:10:49,549 --> 00:10:51,440
She went to work.

217
00:10:51,440 --> 00:10:52,872
I see.

218
00:10:53,504 --> 00:10:55,255
How was the museum?

219
00:10:55,255 --> 00:10:57,524
It was amazing.

220
00:10:57,524 --> 00:11:01,720
You know, there was a painting
of a bridge in the sky,

221
00:11:01,720 --> 00:11:05,599
surrounded by clouds in a bright red sunset.

222
00:11:05,599 --> 00:11:10,170
Man, I want you to see it too, Nat.

223
00:11:10,170 --> 00:11:12,739
Okay.

224
00:11:12,739 --> 00:11:15,300
Oh, a quiz question.

225
00:11:15,300 --> 00:11:16,960
What? Why so suddenly?

226
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:20,200
Why are summer sunsets so red?

227
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:23,550
Because in summer,
there's more water vapor in the air.

228
00:11:23,550 --> 00:11:26,688
Correct! You really know
your stuff about the sky.

229
00:11:26,688 --> 00:11:28,720
That was easy.

230
00:11:28,720 --> 00:11:30,624
Don't underestimate me.

231
00:11:30,624 --> 00:11:32,659
Nat, are you a delinquent?

232
00:11:32,659 --> 00:11:35,456
What? No, I'm not. I'm not a poser.

233
00:11:35,456 --> 00:11:39,840
What? What does "poser" mean?

234
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:42,600
Huh? You don't know?

235
00:11:45,576 --> 00:11:48,446
- I'm home.
- Sorry to intrude.

236
00:11:48,446 --> 00:11:51,392
Huh? Is Rock not here?

237
00:11:55,519 --> 00:11:57,822
- Natsuki, welcome back.
- I'm home.

238
00:11:57,822 --> 00:11:59,624
Welcome, Souta.

239
00:11:59,624 --> 00:12:01,125
Thanks for having me again today.

240
00:12:01,125 --> 00:12:03,494
Thank you for coming.

241
00:12:03,494 --> 00:12:05,196
Mom, where's Rock?

242
00:12:05,196 --> 00:12:07,197
He's probably sleeping over there, right?

243
00:12:16,474 --> 00:12:17,816
He's not there.

244
00:12:17,816 --> 00:12:19,744
No way!

245
00:12:19,744 --> 00:12:21,879
Maybe he went for a walk with Dad?

246
00:12:21,879 --> 00:12:26,444
Your dad got called out by Fuku
to go drinking together.

247
00:12:26,444 --> 00:12:28,946
- What?
- What?

248
00:12:29,620 --> 00:12:31,232
Rock!

249
00:12:33,057 --> 00:12:34,791
Rock!

250
00:12:35,626 --> 00:12:36,994
- Was he there?
- No.

251
00:12:36,994 --> 00:12:38,488
- He's nowhere to be found.
- What? What?

252
00:12:38,488 --> 00:12:40,765
- What? No way.
- This is weird.

253
00:12:40,765 --> 00:12:42,200
Oh wait.

254
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:43,944
- Rock?
- Rock!

255
00:12:43,944 --> 00:12:46,656
Rock, why?

256
00:12:47,705 --> 00:12:51,008
Well... let's calm down and think.

257
00:12:51,008 --> 00:12:53,511
You're right, you're right.

258
00:12:53,511 --> 00:12:56,647
Ma'am, have you been home this whole time?

259
00:12:56,647 --> 00:12:59,617
I went shopping
and just got back a little while ago.

260
00:12:59,617 --> 00:13:01,564
When you got back, was Rock here?

261
00:13:01,564 --> 00:13:02,687
No.

262
00:13:02,687 --> 00:13:06,090
I'm home. Rock?

263
00:13:06,090 --> 00:13:08,504
<i>He didn't come to greet me.</i>

264
00:13:08,504 --> 00:13:10,944
But you know, when he's fast asleep
in the bedroom,

265
00:13:10,944 --> 00:13:12,663
he doesn't always come out.

266
00:13:12,663 --> 00:13:17,435
So I thought I shouldn't disturb him,
so I didn't check.

267
00:13:17,435 --> 00:13:19,424
Okay, then before that,

268
00:13:19,424 --> 00:13:21,496
when you went out shopping, was he here?

269
00:13:21,496 --> 00:13:22,552
Yes.

270
00:13:22,552 --> 00:13:23,574
See you later.

271
00:13:23,574 --> 00:13:25,472
<i>He saw me off at the door.</i>

272
00:13:27,311 --> 00:13:32,224
So that means he disappeared
while you were out shopping.

273
00:13:34,852 --> 00:13:36,654
- What?
- Did you remember something?

274
00:13:36,654 --> 00:13:38,264
The key!

275
00:13:38,264 --> 00:13:42,426
I was planning to come back right away,
so I left without locking the door.

276
00:13:42,426 --> 00:13:43,961
So Rock...

277
00:13:43,961 --> 00:13:46,968
Can Rock open the door by himself?

278
00:13:46,968 --> 00:13:49,440
- No, he can't do that.
- Or maybe someone opened the door

279
00:13:49,440 --> 00:13:51,044
and he ran out?

280
00:13:51,044 --> 00:13:54,171
Or did someone come in and take him?

281
00:13:54,171 --> 00:13:57,641
But he wouldn't just go
with a stranger, would he?

282
00:13:57,641 --> 00:13:59,443
He might.

283
00:13:59,443 --> 00:14:00,664
Rock is so friendly.

284
00:14:00,664 --> 00:14:03,380
It's my fault... What should we do?

285
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:04,710
What if he ran outside

286
00:14:04,710 --> 00:14:07,296
- and got into an accident?
- Please calm down.

287
00:14:10,187 --> 00:14:12,424
Let's search the area first.

288
00:14:12,424 --> 00:14:16,684
Ma'am, please stay here,
in case someone contacts you.

289
00:14:16,684 --> 00:14:17,762
But...

290
00:14:17,762 --> 00:14:21,248
It's okay, leave it to us.

291
00:14:24,735 --> 00:14:27,008
Come on, Nat, let's go.

292
00:14:30,474 --> 00:14:31,744
Let's go!

293
00:14:35,044 --> 00:14:37,214
Rock!

294
00:14:37,214 --> 00:14:40,184
- Rock!
- Hey! Rock!

295
00:14:40,184 --> 00:14:42,953
Let's try searching over there too, Nat.

296
00:14:44,655 --> 00:14:47,091
- Rock!
- Nat,

297
00:14:47,091 --> 00:14:49,125
show her the photo.

298
00:14:50,060 --> 00:14:51,629
Have you seen this dog?

299
00:14:51,629 --> 00:14:53,264
Isn't that Rock?

300
00:14:53,264 --> 00:14:56,600
- Do you know anything?
- I haven't seen him today.

301
00:14:56,600 --> 00:14:58,064
- I see.
- Right.

302
00:14:58,064 --> 00:14:59,136
Nat!

303
00:14:59,136 --> 00:15:00,152
Rock!

304
00:15:00,152 --> 00:15:02,624
- Thank you very much.
- No problem.

305
00:15:02,624 --> 00:15:03,968
Rock!

306
00:15:05,112 --> 00:15:06,420
Rock!

307
00:15:11,064 --> 00:15:12,308
Rock!

308
00:15:14,136 --> 00:15:15,355
Rock!

309
00:15:27,288 --> 00:15:28,640
Natsuki!

310
00:15:30,267 --> 00:15:31,502
How did it go?

311
00:15:31,502 --> 00:15:33,792
No information. What about you?

312
00:15:36,774 --> 00:15:38,642
Let's try over there.

313
00:15:38,642 --> 00:15:40,544
I'll let you know if I hear anything.

314
00:15:40,544 --> 00:15:43,104
- Please do.
- Thanks.

315
00:15:52,723 --> 00:15:55,744
Any word from the police station, Nat?

316
00:15:59,597 --> 00:16:01,984
Let's search over there.

317
00:16:06,937 --> 00:16:08,288
Nat?

318
00:16:12,009 --> 00:16:14,592
[Lost Property Receipt Card]
Why is Rock treated as lost property?

319
00:16:16,313 --> 00:16:17,947
What?

320
00:16:19,617 --> 00:16:23,392
We filed a lost property report
at the police station just now.

321
00:16:25,322 --> 00:16:26,956
Nat...

322
00:16:30,327 --> 00:16:31,904
He's not a thing.

323
00:16:34,131 --> 00:16:36,832
Rock is family...

324
00:16:51,181 --> 00:16:55,584
Anyway, let's just search for now.

325
00:16:59,160 --> 00:17:00,448
Let's go.

326
00:17:08,440 --> 00:17:09,728
It's okay.

327
00:17:14,888 --> 00:17:16,757
Have you seen this dog?

328
00:17:16,757 --> 00:17:19,228
- No.
- No, we haven't seen him.

329
00:17:19,228 --> 00:17:21,988
I see. Thank you very much.

330
00:17:27,612 --> 00:17:31,076
Where on earth did Rock go?

331
00:17:38,845 --> 00:17:41,372
Should we hire a pet detective?

332
00:17:41,372 --> 00:17:45,886
There are professionals
who search for lost dogs and cats.

333
00:17:45,886 --> 00:17:47,940
I think I saw it on TV.

334
00:17:49,120 --> 00:17:51,160
[Pet Detective FAST]
Found it.

335
00:18:04,938 --> 00:18:07,076
- Huh?
- What?

336
00:18:10,908 --> 00:18:12,324
Rock?

337
00:18:21,021 --> 00:18:22,436
Rock!

338
00:18:25,212 --> 00:18:26,500
Rock!

339
00:18:28,495 --> 00:18:30,297
Rock!

340
00:18:30,297 --> 00:18:32,232
Thank goodness! Rock!

341
00:18:32,232 --> 00:18:33,900
Riyo?

342
00:18:35,068 --> 00:18:36,708
What? Sis?

343
00:18:38,772 --> 00:18:39,873
Why?

344
00:18:39,873 --> 00:18:41,828
What do you mean, why? I'm walking him.

345
00:18:43,516 --> 00:18:44,811
What are you doing?

346
00:18:44,811 --> 00:18:46,340
Huh? Why are you crying?

347
00:18:48,181 --> 00:18:51,384
Because Rock was gone,

348
00:18:51,384 --> 00:18:53,092
and we couldn't find him anywhere!

349
00:18:54,076 --> 00:18:56,890
What? I have no idea what's going on.

350
00:18:56,890 --> 00:18:59,452
Rock wasn't home, so we were looking for him.

351
00:18:59,452 --> 00:19:00,560
Why?

352
00:19:00,560 --> 00:19:04,140
- We thought you were at work.
- That's right.

353
00:19:04,140 --> 00:19:05,880
Huh? Must've been a misunderstanding.

354
00:19:05,880 --> 00:19:08,900
I didn't have a shift today,
so I came straight home.

355
00:19:08,900 --> 00:19:11,044
And then Rock looked bored,
so I took him out.

356
00:19:13,173 --> 00:19:16,510
Nat and your mom were so worried.

357
00:19:16,510 --> 00:19:18,512
Ah, sorry, sorry.

358
00:19:18,512 --> 00:19:21,188
I'm so glad you're safe, Rock.

359
00:19:22,916 --> 00:19:24,644
- Rock!
- Rock!

360
00:19:25,318 --> 00:19:27,053
Are you okay?

361
00:19:27,053 --> 00:19:30,756
Rock! Where have you been?

362
00:19:42,169 --> 00:19:43,620
Are you okay?

363
00:19:44,237 --> 00:19:46,532
Yeah, I'm fine.

364
00:19:49,810 --> 00:19:53,680
From now on, I'll definitely lock the door
whenever I leave the house.

365
00:19:53,680 --> 00:19:59,252
Well, even though that wasn't
the cause this time, please do that.

366
00:19:59,252 --> 00:20:00,987
Please.

367
00:20:00,987 --> 00:20:03,947
I grew up in the countryside,
so I sometimes forget,

368
00:20:03,947 --> 00:20:06,308
but I definitely won't do that again.

369
00:20:08,668 --> 00:20:09,956
Rock.

370
00:20:10,797 --> 00:20:12,799
Speaking of which, what were you doing, Dad?

371
00:20:12,799 --> 00:20:14,668
He went drinking with Fuku.

372
00:20:14,668 --> 00:20:16,240
Again?

373
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:19,506
If you'd been home, Dad,
this wouldn't have happened.

374
00:20:19,506 --> 00:20:22,708
- I know, right?
- It's true.

375
00:20:24,720 --> 00:20:26,479
I see.

376
00:20:26,479 --> 00:20:28,900
Well... I'm sorry.

377
00:20:31,380 --> 00:20:32,919
Okay, help me out here.

378
00:20:32,919 --> 00:20:35,288
- Let's have some tea.
- Maybe I'll have another drink.

379
00:20:35,288 --> 00:20:38,084
- What? You're drinking more?
- Just a little more.

380
00:20:55,942 --> 00:20:57,412
So fluffy!

381
00:21:06,753 --> 00:21:08,387
Oh, right.

382
00:21:09,276 --> 00:21:10,628
[Great job]
Here you go.

383
00:21:15,128 --> 00:21:17,860
But we didn't have a lesson today.

384
00:21:17,860 --> 00:21:20,164
But you worked hard searching for Rock.

385
00:21:26,339 --> 00:21:27,620
You don't want it?

386
00:21:29,409 --> 00:21:31,108
This is from me.

387
00:21:31,711 --> 00:21:33,079
What?

388
00:21:33,079 --> 00:21:36,420
Mom and I just panicked.

389
00:21:37,617 --> 00:21:39,318
So...

390
00:21:42,622 --> 00:21:46,212
If you hadn't been there, Sou,
it would've been bad.

391
00:21:47,928 --> 00:21:51,076
So, this is a thank-you.

392
00:21:54,901 --> 00:21:57,860
I was only able to stay calm
because I'm not family.

393
00:21:59,172 --> 00:22:02,920
By the way, I saw that you were
finally able to touch Rock.

394
00:22:02,920 --> 00:22:05,924
Right! He was so fluffy. I was surprised.

395
00:22:06,844 --> 00:22:08,196
You did a great job.

396
00:22:10,050 --> 00:22:11,268
I see.

397
00:22:12,919 --> 00:22:15,322
All right, then I'll take this one.

398
00:22:15,322 --> 00:22:16,548
And...

399
00:22:17,924 --> 00:22:19,364
This is for you, Nat.

400
00:22:20,827 --> 00:22:24,030
It's fine, I don't have anywhere
to put it right now.

401
00:22:24,030 --> 00:22:25,664
Then...

402
00:22:31,996 --> 00:22:33,252
Right here.

403
00:22:38,236 --> 00:22:43,108
[Great job]

404
00:22:47,387 --> 00:22:49,789
I'm not a kid.

405
00:22:50,640 --> 00:22:52,826
- Natsuki, are you awake?
- I'm sleeping.

406
00:22:52,826 --> 00:22:54,227
Huh? But you're awake now, aren't you?

407
00:22:54,227 --> 00:22:55,929
What is it?

408
00:22:55,929 --> 00:22:58,349
This is a souvenir. I found it in Ueno.

409
00:22:58,349 --> 00:23:00,767
Since I'm always borrowing your stuff.

410
00:23:00,767 --> 00:23:02,268
Ta-da!

411
00:23:02,268 --> 00:23:04,738
- Nice! I like it.
- Right?

412
00:23:04,738 --> 00:23:08,560
You really do like
the same things I like, Natsuki.

413
00:23:08,560 --> 00:23:10,660
- That's not true.
- Let me borrow it sometime, okay?

414
00:23:14,180 --> 00:23:19,204
<i>I like the same things my sister likes.</i>

